-11-11", "summary": "A study presented at the American Heart Association's Scientific Sessions 2026 found energy drinks and stimulant supplements associated with 11× more cardiac arrest reports and 4.5× more heart attack reports. Young adults ages 18–34 comprised nearly half of severe cases; some products contain 3–12× ", "takeaways": ["Energy drinks/stimulants vs. products without: 11× cardiac arrest reports, 4.5× heart attack reports", "Young adults (18–34): nearly 50% of severe cardiovascular emergencies", "Some energy drinks: 3× coffee's caffeine per fluid ounce; supplements 12× coffee's concentration", "FDA classifies as foods/supplements, exempting from drug safety testing requirements", "Energy drink industry sales 2024: $20+ billion (double from decade prior)"], "sources": [{"label": "ScienceDaily", "url": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261110042543.htm", "origin": "research"}, {"label": "ScienceDaily — Health", "url": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261110042543.htm", "origin": "rss"}, {"label": "ScienceDaily — Nutrition", "url": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261110042543.htm", "origin": "rss"}], "subfeeds": [{"key": "diet-exercise", "title": "Diet & Exercise"}, {"key": "health", "title": "Health"}], "feeds": [{"key": "science", "title": "Science"}], "researched": true, "receivedAt": "2026-11-11T20:58:43.426875+00:00", "relatedTitle": "", "relatedUrl": "", "updatesTitle": "", "updatesUrl": ""}, {"title": "Occasional marijuana use linked to 40% higher stroke risk", "url": "news/diet-exercise/2026-11-11/#occasional-marijuana-use-linked-to-40-higher-stroke-risk", "importance": 7, "date": "2026-11-11", "summary": "A study of 440,000+ Americans presented at the American Heart Association's Scientific Sessions 2026 found occasional marijuana use associated with 40% higher odds of reporting stroke history. The association held across consumption methods and was not limited to frequent users.", "takeaways": ["Occasion